.TH "RAPTOR-FEV" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-fev \- Fail things and read the effects (Failure Effects View).
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor fev\fR [\-h] [\-\-phase N] [\-\-fail SEL] [\-\-repair SEL] [\-\-cycle SEL] [\-\-script FILE] [\-\-log FILE] [\-f {text,json}] [\-\-criticality] [\-\-capacity] MODEL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fail things and read the effects (Failure Effects View).
Start from the all\-operating state (phase 1 of a phased model), apply the actions, and print the Failure Effects text. Nothing is simulated and no random number is drawn. Actions run in this order: \-\-phase, \-\-fail, \-\-repair, \-\-cycle; use \-\-script for any other order (see the script actions in raptor\-fev(1)).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-phase\fR \fIN\fR
go to phase N first (phased models)
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\fR \fISEL\fR
fail a block or event (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-repair\fR \fISEL\fR
repair a failed block or event (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-cycle\fR \fISEL\fR
click an element, as the mouse does: cycles a hatched (induced) block (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-script\fR \fIFILE\fR
read actions from FILE, one per line (\- for stdin); each `write` line records the text at that point
.TP
\fB\-\-log\fR \fIFILE\fR
write the Raptor 7\-format Failure Effects log (CRLF, the file Write To Failure Effects Log appends to)
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-criticality\fR
add the Criticality line (Raptor 7's developer option)
.TP
\fB\-\-capacity\fR
also show the flow delivered, and the flow and capacity of each capacity node (models with capacity analysis; not in Raptor 7)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Fail one block and read what it does to the system.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor fev pump.rbd \-\-fail 'Pump A'\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
The same in phase 3, as JSON.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor fev plane.rbd \-\-phase 3 \-\-fail Hydraulics \-f json\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replay a click script; every `write` line adds one block to the log, as Write To Failure Effects Log does.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor fev plane.rbd \-\-script session.fev \-\-log fevlog.txt\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
.SH SCRIPT ACTIONS
One action per line in a \fB--script\fR file; blank lines and text after \fB#\fR are ignored. The names are the elements' names or numeric ids.
.TP
\fBclick\fR
left\-click a block or event (cycles a hatched block)
.TP
\fBfail\fR
click an operating block, or an event that has not failed
.TP
\fBrepair\fR
click a failed or PM block, or a failed event
.TP
\fBphase\fR
go to phase N
.TP
\fBnext\fR
the forward phase arrow (wraps)
.TP
\fBprev\fR
the back phase arrow (wraps)
.TP
\fBerase\fR
the large eraser: everything operating, phase 1
.TP
\fBerase\-phase\fR
the small eraser: clear failures, keep the phase
.TP
\fBwrite\fR
Write To Failure Effects Log: record the text now
